1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,585
The Curiosity Club.

2
00:00:02,585 --> 00:00:04,943
Episode 12.

3
00:00:04,943 --> 00:00:07,926
The Bird That Flies Underwater.

4
00:00:07,926 --> 00:00:10,951
Here is something to listen for.

5
00:00:10,951 --> 00:00:15,312
Does a penguin stop being a bird because it cannot fly?

6
00:00:15,312 --> 00:00:16,903
Ready?

7
00:00:16,903 --> 00:00:19,105
Let us find out.

8
00:00:19,105 --> 00:00:22,343
Leo is making an animal quiz.

9
00:00:22,343 --> 00:00:26,164
His first rule says: All birds can fly.

10
00:00:26,164 --> 00:00:29,957
Maya points to a penguin in a nature video.

11
00:00:29,957 --> 00:00:32,088
What about that one?

12
00:00:32,088 --> 00:00:34,985
It is swimming, Leo says.

13
00:00:34,985 --> 00:00:38,366
Perhaps it is a fish wearing a jacket.

14
00:00:38,366 --> 00:00:41,434
Pip checks his picture library.

15
00:00:41,434 --> 00:00:43,778
Jacket detected.

16
00:00:43,778 --> 00:00:46,463
Fish status uncertain.

17
00:00:46,463 --> 00:00:50,170
Ms. Park explains that penguins are birds.

18
00:00:50,170 --> 00:00:53,892
They have feathers, breathe air, and lay eggs.

19
00:00:53,892 --> 00:00:58,778
Their wings are shaped for moving through water instead of flying through air.

20
00:00:58,778 --> 00:01:03,849
The penguin in the video dives, turns, and speeds after a fish.

21
00:01:03,849 --> 00:01:06,846
On land, it had looked awkward.

22
00:01:06,846 --> 00:01:10,426
Underwater, it looks quick and graceful.

23
00:01:10,426 --> 00:01:14,190
It almost seems to fly down there, Maya says.

24
00:01:14,190 --> 00:01:20,383
That is a useful description, says Ms. Park, as long as we remember it is swimming.

25
00:01:20,383 --> 00:01:23,309
Leo changes his quiz rule.

26
00:01:23,309 --> 00:01:26,690
Many birds fly, but some do not.

27
00:01:26,690 --> 00:01:29,488
Then he adds another question.

28
00:01:29,488 --> 00:01:32,997
Do all penguins live on Antarctic ice?

29
00:01:32,997 --> 00:01:37,968
Ms. Park shows them penguins on a rocky coast far from Antarctica.

30
00:01:37,968 --> 00:01:41,491
Different species live in different places.

31
00:01:41,491 --> 00:01:45,028
Pip tapes paper flippers onto his sides.

32
00:01:45,028 --> 00:01:48,352
Do not try swimming, Maya tells him.

33
00:01:48,352 --> 00:01:51,079
You are a classroom robot.

34
00:01:51,079 --> 00:01:53,522
I know, says Pip.

35
00:01:53,522 --> 00:01:57,017
These are for my very dry penguin dance.

36
00:01:57,017 --> 00:02:03,650
Leo writes the final quiz question: Which member of our club should definitely stay out of the pool?

37
00:02:03,650 --> 00:02:06,803
Now, a little more to discover.

38
00:02:06,803 --> 00:02:11,264
Penguins are flightless birds with wings adapted for swimming.

39
00:02:11,264 --> 00:02:15,994
Their feathers and body features help them live in their environments.

40
00:02:15,994 --> 00:02:20,184
Penguin species do not all live on Antarctic ice.

41
00:02:20,184 --> 00:02:24,985
Being a bird does not require the ability to fly through the air.

42
00:02:24,985 --> 00:02:28,153
Let us hear the main idea again.

43
00:02:28,153 --> 00:02:32,031
Leo's rule that all birds fly needed a correction.

44
00:02:32,031 --> 00:02:36,846
Penguins are birds, but their wings work as flippers underwater.

45
00:02:36,846 --> 00:02:43,210
The club learned to check a category using several features instead of one familiar example.

46
00:02:43,210 --> 00:02:46,349
Here are three useful expressions.

47
00:02:46,349 --> 00:02:49,531
You can listen, or say them with me.

48
00:02:49,531 --> 00:02:52,840
It can swim, but it cannot fly.

49
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:56,150
It can swim, but it cannot fly.

50
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:59,090
This one is different from that one.

51
00:02:59,090 --> 00:03:02,031
This one is different from that one.

52
00:03:02,031 --> 00:03:04,602
Does every bird do that?

53
00:03:04,602 --> 00:03:07,173
Does every bird do that?

54
00:03:07,173 --> 00:03:10,170
Remember our listening question?

55
00:03:10,170 --> 00:03:14,531
Does a penguin stop being a bird because it cannot fly?

56
00:03:14,531 --> 00:03:16,818
Here is the answer.

57
00:03:16,818 --> 00:03:18,480
No.

58
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:24,502
Penguins are birds even though their wings are adapted for swimming rather than flight in the air.

59
00:03:24,502 --> 00:03:28,465
And here is a question just for your imagination.

60
00:03:28,465 --> 00:03:33,238
Can you think of another group whose members do not all do the same thing?

61
00:03:33,238 --> 00:03:36,548
There is more than one possible answer.

62
00:03:36,548 --> 00:03:39,843
Keep wondering, and see you next time.
